  "body": " Lifting the orientation-preserving abelian automorphisms   The natural map is surjective. More explicitly, every element of has the unique form with and , and every lifts to .    We first determine the orientation-preserving automorphisms of the abelianization, then realize their unit-scaling part, and finally realize the remaining shear.  Because , the element topologically generates . From and one obtains The torsion subgroup of is the order-two group generated by . Hence an orientation-preserving automorphism fixes , sends to for a unique unit , and sends to for a unique . Conversely, every map is an orientation-preserving automorphism of .   In more detail: the fact that the coefficient is a unit is not an extra assumption in the classification. Applying the same row extraction to an automorphism and to its inverse produces coefficients and with . Preservation of the order-two element then forces the -row once the -row is known.  The automorphism of sends to , so it fixes and sends to . The canonical orientation is the action on the dualizing module and is therefore preserved by every automorphism of . Thus induces for some .   For the lift, the formal proof makes a small coordinate correction explicit. If sends to , then composing with a shear of parameter contributes , not , after the unit scaling. Thus one takes . The inverse shear has parameter , so this construction gives an automorphism rather than only an endomorphism.  For , define Here is conjugation, not the product . This is an automorphism of the free pro- group on , with inverse . Moreover and therefore It therefore descends to an automorphism of , inducing . The composite induces , proving surjectivity.   "
