  "title": "Regular-module realization of the base local connecting map.",
  "body": " Regular-module realization of the base local connecting map   With notation as in , the base local determinant form satisfies, for every , Under Kummer theory and the normalized Shapiro cochain map , the right side is obtained by applying the orbit operations of to the scalar Shapiro coordinates. Thus the regular-module computation evaluates the actual base equivariant central class , including the -terms ; it is not merely a polynomial with the same polarization .   Lean   The equality of classes is the pullback identity from . Pulling that identity back along a Galois graph cocycle gives equality of normalized central -cocycles over , hence after applying the local invariant map .  For the second assertion, use the explicit representatives in , , and . Direct substitution of the normalized Shapiro cocycle gives the square and free-orbit corestriction formulas . For a half-orbit , the correction term records exactly whether the action on a right coset of preserves or reverses the chosen orientation of its two coordinates. Thus the graph pullback is the normalized corestriction of the two-point graph cocycle ; by that two-point class is the index-two Evens norm . The full cochain calculation is written out in .   "
