  "body": " The orientation of    carries a unique continuous character describing its action on the dualizing module . Its values on the generators are where is the unique root of with , and ; numerically and . Moreover is surjective, with image .   Lean (the character)  Lean (orientation)  Lean (image)   The orientation of a Demushkin group is characterized by the property that every -crossed derivation of the free pro- group kills the relator; see . Evaluating the crossed derivations valued in on the relator of gives three coordinate equations, together with the relation forced by the exponent sums. The branch is excluded, because it forces with a unit, while is inconsistent with the remaining equation. On the branch the system reduces to , which has a unique root congruent to modulo by Hensel's lemma , and then . Surjectivity follows from Burnside's basis theorem applied to the image, together with the fact that is not a square modulo .   "
